From a21de47f1e8eb176d29659fa687db54dc3213204 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:35:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/16] arm64: dts: apple: j716c: Add the right port's
 USB4/Thunderbolt router

Describe the USB4/Thunderbolt host router behind the right-hand USB-C
port (ADT /arm-io/acio2, acio-cpu2 and dart-acio2). In t6050-max.dtsi:

- the ATC2_CIO, ATC2_CIO_PCIE, ATC2_CIO_USB and ATC2_CIO_AUSS power
  domains;
- the router CPU's mailbox and the router's LSTX pin function on the
  AOP GPIO controller;
- the router itself, with its DART and NHI as children, so that both
  are populated only once the router runs: nothing is touched at boot;
- the DART's stream 15 in bypass, full error reporting and the context
  cache flush.

In the board: AUSS, kept as the boot loader leaves it, the CIO reconfig
request (port 2 of the die's CIO reset), the AOP GPIO controller with
only the LSTX pin exposed, the PHY's CIO80 RX_TOP tunables, the link
from the PD controller to the router, and, until the boot loader fills
them, this board's router, NHI and DART tunables and host DROM, from its
ADT.

The router node is named acio@: the boot loader disables a cio@ node
unless its first register is the third register of the matching
/arm-io/acioN, which on T6050 is not the router's rc block.

Developed with Claude Code.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
